== Notes ==

*Monks lose some abilities while wearing [[armor]] or using a [[shield]], but ''flurry of blows'' is not one of them; it works with armor and shield.
*This feat can be used with [[druid]] shapes that do not use [[weapon]]s.
*When dual-wielding, both weapons must be kamas in order to activate this feat.
* Unlike other combat modes, ''flurry of blows'' activates instantly (in the middle of a combat round). However, only the penalties are applied immediately; the extra attack only occurs when an entire round elapses with this mode active.

=== Previous versions ===

*Prior to version 1.69, this feat could be used when wielding a weapon other than a kama in the off-hand, as long as the main-hand weapon was a kama.

==Builder notes==

'''Item feat:''' No, but it can be added with custom content.

==Custom content notes==

'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' No. The interface is hardcoded to the monk class alone, so the other classes cannot reach it.

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*This feat can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] to make it available as an item feat. But this is pointless if the feat acquirement list for monks is not changed.